  <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-950 mt-10 mb-4">1. The Energy Math: Gasoline Inefficiency vs. Electric Motor Dominance</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    To understand why an electric car costs so much less to operate, one must look at basic physics. Internal combustion engines (ICE) are fundamentally inefficient heat generators that happen to move a vehicle. Only <strong>20% to 30%</strong> of the chemical energy contained within a gallon or liter of gasoline is converted into kinetic motion at the wheels. The remaining 70% to 80% is completely lost as radiant heat through the engine block, exhaust pipe, and radiator.
  </p>
  <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    By contrast, modern permanent magnet and induction electric motors operate at <strong>85% to 92% thermodynamic efficiency</strong>. Virtually every kilowatt-hour of electric current drawn from the battery pack is delivered directly to the drivetrain.
  </p>

