  <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-950 mt-10 mb-4">2. Maintenance: The Hidden Drain on Combustion Ownership</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    When prospective car buyers compare a petrol vehicle to an EV on a dealership lot, they almost always fixate exclusively on the monthly fuel budget. However, long-term fleet tracking data proves that mechanical maintenance is often where the most dramatic cumulative savings occur.
  </p>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    A standard internal combustion powertrain contains over <strong>2,000 moving components</strong> that operate under intense friction, explosive pressure, and thermal stress. Over a 5-year ownership cycle, an ICE vehicle requires:
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mb-6 space-y-2 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-800">
    <li>10 to 15 synthetic engine oil and filter replacements</li>
    <li>Engine air filter and cabin filter replacements</li>
    <li>Spark plug and ignition coil servicing</li>
    <li>Transmission fluid flush, torque converter, or clutch plate replacements</li>
    <li>Serpentine belts, timing belts, and water pump overhauls</li>
    <li>Catalytic converter and exhaust oxygen sensor maintenance</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    An electric powertrain eliminates approximately <strong>95% of these mechanical failure points</strong>. An electric motor contains fewer than 20 moving parts, utilizes a single-speed reduction transmission with zero clutches, and uses no motor oil. Routine EV maintenance is essentially reduced to cabin air filter replacements, tire rotations, and windshield wiper fluid.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-950 mt-10 mb-4">3. Regenerative Braking: 3x Longer Brake Pad Lifespan</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    One of the least publicized yet most impactful cost advantages of an electric vehicle is <strong>regenerative braking</strong>. In a traditional vehicle, every time you press the brake pedal, kinetic motion is turned into wasted heat by pressing ceramic pads against spinning iron brake rotors. Consequently, brake pads must be replaced every 25,000 to 45,000 kilometers.
  </p>
  <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    In an EV, releasing the accelerator reverses the magnetic polarity of the electric motor, transforming it into a high-capacity electric generator that slows the vehicle down while funneling harvested energy back into the battery. Friction brakes are rarely engaged during normal driving. As a result, EV brake pads frequently last over <strong>100,000 to 150,000 kilometers</strong> before requiring inspection or replacement.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-950 mt-10 mb-4">4. The 5-Year Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) Break-Even</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    Because an EV carries a higher upfront acquisition cost due to battery pack chemistry manufacturing, the key question is: <em>At what mileage does an EV break even and pay for itself?</em>
  </p>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    For the average urban commuter driving between 40 to 60 kilometers per day (approximately 15,000 to 20,000 km annually), the typical break-even timeline is <strong>2.5 to 3.5 years</strong>. From year 4 onward, every kilometer traveled generates pure discretionary financial savings that stay in your bank account.
  </p>
  <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    For ride-hail operators, taxi drivers, and daily delivery couriers traveling 100+ km daily, the break-even is achieved in as little as <strong>12 to 18 months</strong>!
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-950 mt-10 mb-4">5. What About Two-Wheelers and Motorcycles?</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    If you commute on a motorcycle or scooter, the savings ratio is even more immediate. Electric bikes offer an astonishing 30 to 45 km per kWh, allowing you to commute an entire month for the price of a single tank of petrol. Explore our dedicated analysis: <a href="/blog/ev-bikes-2026" class="text-emerald-600 font-bold hover:underline">Are Electric Motorcycles Worth It in 2026?</a>
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-950 mt-10 mb-4">6. Battery Health & Degradation Concerns</h2>
